	(footprint "picoemp:SOP-6_LDA111"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "66a16ef9-dd90-4752-9fb0-285874fad5e4")
		(at 124.4 131.1 90)
		(descr "Littelfuse LDA111STR, SOP-6 gull-wing (SamacSys SOP254P952X470-6N), 2.54mm pitch, body height 4.70mm max. Pad centres and pitch taken from the original ChipShouter-Pico footprint on the as-received board, but pad rotation was corrected: the source Altium->KiCad import had the 2.54mm pad dimension along the 2.54mm pitch axis, fusing adjacent pads into one solid bar with zero gap. Here the 2.54mm dimension runs along X (toe-to-heel, away from the body) and 1.27mm along Y, leaving a 1.27mm gap between adjacent pads. Pin 3 is electrically NC but its lead physically exists -- pad 3 is included so the lead isn't left unsoldered.")
