	(footprint "picoemp:SMA_Linx_CONSMA020_062_G_EdgeMount"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "d8fa6a7d-6b26-4c5a-818f-4e88e55469f9")
		(at 124.39 175.272 90)
		(descr "TE Connectivity / Linx CONSMA020.062-G -- SMA jack (female socket), PCB edge mount, end launch, 50 ohm, for 0.062 in (1.57 mm) board. 500 V RMS, DC-18 GHz, -65 to +165 C. Land pattern taken from the recommended footprint on sheet 2 of ENG_DS_L9000279-01_A: centre pad 5.60 x 1.50, four ground pads 4.90 x 1.60 on a 8.52 mm pitch (+/-4.26), grounds on both copper layers because the connector straddles the board edge. ORIGIN IS AT THE BOARD EDGE, +X pointing into the board -- place the origin on Edge.Cuts. Copper is set back 0.100 mm from the origin so it does not overlap the edge graphic; KiCad flags a coincident pad even under a 0 mm edge rule, and fabs cannot plate right to a routed edge anyway. The stock Amphenol footprint uses the same trick with 0.090 mm. DigiKey 343-CONSMA020.062-G-ND.")
		(tags "SMA edge mount end launch RF coaxial linx TE")
