	(footprint "picoemp:TerminalBlock_Phoenix_MKDSN-1,5-2-5.08_1x02_P5.08mm_Horizontal"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "e7c2065e-9bd7-4d99-a246-8d5013974cd0")
		(at 132.6 158 90)
		(descr "Phoenix Contact MKDSN 1,5/2-5,08 -- COMBICON Terminals S, 2 positions, 5.08 mm pitch, horizontal wire entry (0 deg), screw with tension sleeve. Body 10.16 (w) x 8.15 (l) x 13.5 (h), installed height 10, solder pin 3.5 long, pin 0.5 x 1.0, PCB hole 1.3. Insulation coordination per IEC 60664-1: 630 V at II/2, 400 V at III/2, 250 V at III/3, 4 kV rated surge throughout; material group I, CTI 600, clearance 3, creepage 3.2. cULus 300 V / 10 A, VDE 400 V / 17.5 A. Copper is identical to the stock MKDS footprint (1.3 drill, 2.6 pad, 5.08 pitch) so it is drop-in on that land. NOTE: the datasheet gives body depth 8.15 but does not publish where the pins sit within it; the outline here keeps the rear edge where the MKDS had it and pulls the front in by 1.65. That affects silk and courtyard only, never copper. Item 1548128 (SPE variant).")
		(tags "THT terminal block Phoenix MKDSN COMBICON pitch 5.08mm")
